#
# Counter-example for the math:PersistenceModule frame (issue #1527): a math:PersistenceModule
# naming its math:moduleIndex but omitting any math:structureMap — the functor has vector spaces
# but no functorial transition maps. The min-1 qualified restriction on math:structureMap derives
# a sh:qualifiedMinCount property shape, so validation MUST emit
# shacl.QualifiedMinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:IncompletePersistenceModule).
# ISOLATION: the math:moduleIndex arm is satisfied, so only the math:structureMap arm fires; the
# node is not also a math:PersistenceLifetime, so math:PersistenceModuleLifetimeConflation stays silent.
# Back-reference: math:IncompletePersistenceModule (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecPersistenceModuleIncomplete).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:module a math:PersistenceModule ;
    math:moduleIndex ex:indexPoset .             # names the index but NO math:structureMap

ex:indexPoset a math:MathematicalObject .
